{"name":"Purple Pride","hex":"#a274b5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"},{"term":"pride","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The quality or state of being proud.\nA sense of one's own worth; reasonable self-esteem and satisfaction (in oneself, in one's work, one's family, etc).","A sense of one's own worth; reasonable self-esteem and satisfaction (in oneself, in one's work, one's family, etc)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take or experience pride in something; to be proud of it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pride"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pride","blocks":[{"text":"Pride is a primary emotion characterized by a sense of security with one's identity, performance, and/or accomplishments. Depending on the context, pride may be viewed as either a virtue or a vice. Typically, pride arises from praise, independent self-reflection, or a fulfilled feeling of belonging."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Pride_%28Superbia%29%2C_from_The_Seven_Vices_MET_DP867537.jpg/330px-Pride_%28Superbia%29%2C_from_The_Seven_Vices_MET_DP867537.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pride","wikidata":"Q3071551"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple","wikidata":"Q3257809"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Pride%2C_Jacob_Matham.png/250px-Pride%2C_Jacob_Matham.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/29/Pride%2C_Jacob_Matham.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Pride%2C_Jacob_Matham.png/250px-Pride%2C_Jacob_Matham.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pride, from the Seven Deadly Sins by Jacob Matham c. 1592","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APride%2C_Jacob_Matham.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/2016-05-16-Mad_Pride_K%C3%B6ln_2016-4988.jpg/500px-2016-05-16-Mad_Pride_K%C3%B6ln_2016-4988.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/2016-05-16-Mad_Pride_K%C3%B6ln_2016-4988.jpg/1280px-2016-05-16-Mad_Pride_K%C3%B6ln_2016-4988.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/2016-05-16-Mad_Pride_K%C3%B6ln_2016-4988.jpg/500px-2016-05-16-Mad_Pride_K%C3%B6ln_2016-4988.jpg?utm_source=en.wikip